# Frontend environment.
#
# DEV: you normally need NOTHING here. With no env file, the app uses a
# relative `/api/v1` base URL and the Vite dev proxy forwards it to the local
# backend at http://localhost:8000. Start the backend, run `pnpm dev`, done.
#
# If your backend runs elsewhere in dev, either point the proxy at it:
#   VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=http://192.168.4.24:8000
# or bypass the proxy with an absolute base URL:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.4.24:8000/api/v1
#
# PROD (Vercel): set VITE_API_BASE_URL to the absolute backend URL in the
# Vercel project settings, not here.
# PROD (Cloudflare Pages, *.sriadithyafinance.loan): leave VITE_API_BASE_URL
# UNSET. The app then derives each tenant's API from its hostname
# (src/api/baseUrl.ts); setting it would point every tenant at one backend.
